{
  "_comment": [
    "Project aliases for the three environments. ADR-047 makes the build flavor",
    "the environment selector on the app side; this is the same selection for",
    "the Firebase CLI, so a deploy names an environment rather than a project ID",
    "nobody can check at a glance.",
    "",
    "There is deliberately no 'default'. A deploy must say which environment it",
    "means: `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules -P dev`. A default is how a",
    "rules change reaches the wrong project.",
    "",
    "dev IS vump-platform-f86af. Mission 6.4 planned to create a fresh vump-dev",
    "and retire this project; Mission 6.4.2 reversed that. f86af already had",
    "Authentication enabled and Blaze billing linked, and the new vump-dev had",
    "neither and could not be given either from the CLI. vump-dev was deleted.",
    "There is no 'legacy' alias any more, because there is no legacy project —",
    "it is the development environment. Amendment A-162.",
    "",
    "staging and prod exist with Firestore and rules, and are deliberately left",
    "without Auth or billing until a release branch is cut (ADR-014). Deploying",
    "functions to either will fail until then, and that is the intended state."
  ],
  "projects": {
    "dev": "vump-platform-f86af",
    "staging": "vump-staging",
    "prod": "vump-prod"
  }
}
